@*
    OdsSectionDivider — the divider that introduces a band or a section inside a record
    card body (Odyssey Design System · components/SectionDivider).

    A letter-spaced uppercase label, a hairline rule that takes the remaining width,
    and an optional mono meta note on the right ("42 · latest 28 Aug 2026"). Promoted
    from the Insurance page's .ins-sub treatment, which is now the one section divider.

    No icon by design — the label carries it, and a record's sections are already named
    by the header's counts. A section header LABELS, it does not act: sections inside an
    OdsRecordCard body are not collapsible and carry no action slot, because the body
    already opens as a whole and every section-level action belongs to the row menu.

    HeadingLevel puts the label in the heading outline (the client adds this over the
    DS markup, as OdsCollapsible does) — 3 by default, under the record card's own
    level-2 trigger heading. Pass 0 to opt out.
*@

<div class="odc-sectiondivider @Class" id="@Id">
    <span class="odc-sectiondivider-l"
          role="@(HeadingLevel > 0 ? "heading" : null)"
          aria-level="@(HeadingLevel > 0 ? HeadingLevel.ToString(System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) : null)">@Label</span>
    <span class="odc-sectiondivider-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Meta))
    {
        <span class="odc-sectiondivider-meta">@Meta</span>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The section name. Rendered uppercase by the stylesheet — write it in sentence case.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string? Label { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Optional right-aligned mono note: a count, a date, "in force since 12 Mar 2021".</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Meta { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Heading level for the label, so assistive tech can navigate a record body by
    /// section. Default 3 (under the card trigger's level 2); 0 opts out.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int HeadingLevel { get; set; } = 3;

    /// <summary>DOM id — a jump target for an in-body link.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Id { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Extra CSS class(es) appended to the root.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
